gap Consolidation notes list three UNMERGED BRANCH entries (ghost-68937c, ghost-99cffe, ghost-4debb8) whose commits were reported missing from this tree. None of these branch names exist locally, in reflog, or on the remote, so their content cannot be directly inspected. However, direct code review confirms every functional requirement those branches would plausibly have carried (six/five-level enums, migration aliases, persistent-critical mechanism, poller gating, SQLite ack table, chat.rs schema, frontend consolidation) is fully present and working in the current tree — later 'Fix validation issues' commits (87cd279, 49900a9, 44036ab) appear to have re-applied the missing work by other means rather than literal branch merges. Flagging for visibility only; no missing functionality was found.
verdict pass
sum All 5 previously-unmet requirements (FR-5, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-3) are now resolved: merge conflict markers are gone tree-wide, MainApp.tsx's group aggregation uses Math.max over a repo+author-summed per-PR weight (fixing the worst-weight/author-dropped bug), SettingsView/RepoSettingsDrawer/context menus cleanly render all six/five levels from a single shared src/lib/priority.ts source, and both `npm run typecheck` and `cargo build` pass with zero errors (verified by direct re-run, not just the execution log). Combined with the 11 already-accepted requirements, all 13 FRs and 3 NFRs are met. One informational gap noted about unverifiable-but-apparently-moot unmerged branch references.
